@node Intro " Introduction"

This very small (1412 Bytes) AmiExpress XiM Door executes a Batch
called "Logon.Batch" in your BBS: Dir. What it does is, it will
execute a Batch during the Login Sequence, so your LOGOFF.batch
can be reduced to a very small size and safes a lot of time.
Logon.Batch is executed with the RunBack command in your C: Dir
so you can have as much Utils as you want!

@endnode
@node Require " Requirements"

All you need to run this little Util is:

- An Amiga, no matter which model.
- Any Ami- or Sigma-Express version!
- AEDoor.library by SiNTAX/WøT
- RunBack Command in your C: Dir.
- Logon.Batch in your BBS: Dir, protected with +s

Thats all...

@endnode
@node Install " Installation"

- If you don't have the AEDoor.library by SiNTAX/WøT in your LIBS:
  dir already just copy the version included in this archive to your
  LIBS: Dir.

- This little Door also requires the RunBack Command in your C: Dir.
  If you don't have this command just copy my version included in
  this archive to your C: Dir.

- This Door is executed via the FrontEnd.info icon. Either copy
  my FrontEnd.info icon to your BBS:Commands/SYSCmd/ Dir or create
  a new FrontEnd.info icon with the following Tooltypes:

  LOCATION=DOORS:Logon
  TYPE=XIM
  MULTINODE=YES
  STACK=4096
  ACCESS=001

- Now create a Batch called BBS:Logon.Batch and protect it with +s
  for instance: Protect BBS:Logon.Batch +s
 
                        That's it folks ...

  This Util has been tested for a couple of weeks now without any
  crashs or problems at all! Give my Board a Ring and see for yourself!

  Thanks to Joker/ZZC for Beta-Testing!
  
  If you should find any Bugs or have any Suggestions, feel free to
  contact me on PSYCHO TERMiNAL +1(914)682-1975 or via /XNet WHiZ@203001

@endnode
